The review has been written to `docs/reviews/equipment-util/equip-util-01-nd-interpolation.md`.

**Summary**: 5 findings — 1 high, 1 medium, 3 low.

- **High**: Missing index caching/hunting for temporal coherence — the interpolator does a full binary search from scratch on every call, unlike both BTWXT (hypercube caching) and scipy (index caching).
- **Medium**: No query-point validation — NaN/infinite coordinates silently produce garbage outputs.
- **Low**: f32 values storage limits precision; no anisotropic grid tests; `Deserialize` derive bypasses constructor validation.

The multilinear interpolation formula and row-major indexing are **mathematically correct** (verified analytically against BTWXT's weight formulas). Boundary handling via clamping is **safe** (no unbounded extrapolation), and binary search via `partition_point` gives O(log n) per-axis search.
